<title>USA: ANR, Transco plan U.S. gas pipeline.</title>
<headline>ANR, Transco plan U.S. gas pipeline.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>ANR Pipeline Co and Transcontinental Gas Pipe Line Corp said Monday they had signed a letter of intent to form a joint venture to build and run a new natural gas pipeline to serve eastern U.S. states.</p>
<p>ANR, a subsidiary of Coastal Corp, and Transco, a subsidiary of the Williams Cos said the 370-mile pipeline from Defiance, Ohio to Leidy, Pennsylvania would have an initial capacity of up to 900 million cubic feet per day.</p>
</text>
